# The audio is committed. It is what this pack exists to carry, and the
# CurseForge packager builds from a tagged commit -- so a repository without it
# publishes an addon that installs, loads, and is silent, which is worse than
# one that fails. Measured before deciding: git saves 9% on ogg and nothing at
# all between two renderings of the same sentence, so a re-read of the corpus
# adds its full size to history again. That is answered by squashing when it
# happens, not by keeping the audio out.

/release/
/curseforge/
*.zip
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
